Registers one externally implemented source contract by stable type ID.

Registration validates the complete manifest and rejects duplicate IDs;
a later registration can never silently replace the first factory.

One authoritative authorization-state transition observed by the host.

PocketStation classifies only observations supplied by the platform owner;
it never converts a generic backend error into permission state.

First-party CLI realtime nodes retained behind `internal-testing`.

These concrete bounded nodes execute on the realtime plan;
they are not a second runtime and are not part of the stable SDK surface.

Canonical typed configuration handed to a connector sidecar during its
bounded Configure handshake. Secret classification survives the boundary;
Debug output continues to redact secret values.

Full signal contract for a single port.

```
use pocketstation::{SignalSpec, TextFormat};

// Mic audio port
let mic = SignalSpec::audio().with_role("voice");

// Application-defined structured result port
let result = SignalSpec::text(TextFormat::Utf8).with_role("result.partial");
```
